             <div class="col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                 <p>Santan Gopal Pooja is a divinely ordained Anushthan performed to invoke the blessings of Baal Gopal—Lord Krishna in His most innocent and blissful child form. This sacred Pooja acts as a spiritual bridge between divine will and earthly longing, especially for those couples who are earnestly praying for the joy of childbirth and family completeness.</p>
             </div>
             <div class="col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                 <p>As per ancient Vedic wisdom, the desire for a child is not just a biological urge but a soulful yearning, often tied to karmic debts and planetary influences. This Pooja gently clears those invisible blocks, aligning you with the nurturing cosmic energy of motherhood and fatherhood</p>

             </div>
             <div class="col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                 <b>Why Perform Santan Gopal Pooja?</b>
                 <p>This Pooja doesn’t merely seek a child—it calls upon the divine to bless the family with a soul destined to bring joy, peace, and spiritual elevation. Lord Krishna as Baal Gopal is the personification of purity, wisdom, charm, and eternal innocence. His blessings are believed to heal emotional wounds, eliminate fertility-related doshas, and fill the home with divine aura and laughter</p>

             </div>
             <div class="col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                 <b>This Pooja is ideal for those who:</b>
                 <p>Are childless despite years of marriage without medical issues</p>
                 <p>Experience recurrent miscarriages or early pregnancy loss</p>
                 <p>Face emotional disconnect after IVF failures or repeated IUI cycles</p>
                 <p>Have doshas in the 5th house, especially afflicted by Rahu, Shani, or Mangal</p>
                 <p>Women with retrograde or weak Moon/Jupiter in the birth chart</p>
                 <p>Families under Pitru Dosha or Garbha Badha Yog</p>
                 <p>Couples where medical science says “nothing is wrong” – yet hope seems lost</p>

             </div>
             <div class="col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                 <b>Deep Spiritual Benefits:</b>
                 <p>Awakens creative & nurturing energies in the female chart</p>
                 <p>Strengthens Jupiter's blessings (putra karaka) and Moon's emotional stability</p>
                 <p>Clears ancestral blockages (Pitru Dosha) affecting conception</p>
                 <p>Creates a spiritually protective shield around the womb</p>
                 <p>Invites a high-vibration soul into the family, who brings peace & elevation</p>
                 <p>Promotes emotional healing for couples carrying years of pain</p>
                 
             </div>
             <div class="col-md-12 col-lg-12">
                 <b>Who Should Perform This Pooja?</b>
                 <p>Couples facing delays or unexplained difficulties in conceiving</p>
                 <p>Women with a history of pregnancy complications or recurrent miscarriages</p>
                 <p>Those seeking the blessings of a healthy, spiritually blessed child</p>
                 <p>Individuals whose charts reflect doshas in the 5th house, Moon, or Jupiter</p>
                 
